### IntelliJ HTTP Client requests for OrderController
### Usage: open this file in IntelliJ IDEA or VS Code (REST Client) and click the gutter icons to run.

@host = localhost
@port = 8080
@base = http://{{host}}:{{port}}
@basePath = {{base}}/api/orders

### 1) Send a simple order (fire-and-forget)
POST {{basePath}}/simple
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": "ORD-1001",
  "customerId": "CUST-42",
  "amount": 149.99,
  "status": "PENDING",
  "timestamp": "2025-12-07T22:35:00"
}

### 2) Send a priority order (with QoS settings)
POST {{basePath}}/priority
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": "ORD-1002",
  "customerId": "CUST-007",
  "amount": 999.50,
  "status": "PROCESSING",
  "timestamp": "2025-12-07T22:36:00"
}

### 3) Send an order with metadata (region as query parameter)
POST {{basePath}}/with-metadata?region=EU
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": "ORD-1003",
  "customerId": "CUST-77",
  "amount": 75.25,
  "status": "PENDING",
  "timestamp": "2025-12-07T22:37:00"
}

### 4) Receive a single order (if available)
GET {{basePath}}/receive
Accept: application/json

### 5) Process an order synchronously (request-reply)
POST {{basePath}}/process
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "orderId": "ORD-2001",
  "customerId": "CUST-9000",
  "amount": 320.00,
  "status": "PENDING",
  "timestamp": "2025-12-07T22:38:00"
}

### 6) Send bulk express orders (demo action)
POST {{basePath}}/bulk-express
